import workflow as w
c=w.connect();I='I_force_motion';II='II_oscillations_waves';IV='IV_thermodynamics';VI='VI_electric_field';VII='VII_magnetic_field';X='X_wave_optics'
rows=[
(1,'KEEP',[I,X],'data_analysis','Satellite-image timing and cloud-height inference','The original linked 3032x2000 JPEG was acquired, decoded and actually inspected: streets, bridges, shadows and clouds are present. Ground scale/orientation, Sun geometry and shadow parallax permit date/time and altitude inference within ordinary geometry/measurement; uniqueness and projection uncertainties must be discussed, not a missing atmospheric theory.'),
(2,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Escape from a square pond under an explicit pursuer strategy','Swimming/running speeds, square geometry and pursuer response rule are explicit. Kinematics and optimal-path/differential-game mathematics determine guaranteed escape and compare strategies; no specialized physics is required.'),
(3,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Water-driven recoil of a nearly massless cart with a finite outlet tube','Tank/outlet geometry, initial height and negligible hardware mass define a one-dimensional inviscid water-column model. Newton pressure force, continuity and energy/momentum balance including outlet-column inertia yield drainage and cart acceleration. This does not require unsupplied viscous Navier-Stokes dynamics.'),
(4,'KEEP',[I],'numerical','Landing location of vertical launches on a rapidly rotating spherical planet','Inertial launch speed includes local surface rotation; Newton central-force conic and planet rotation give return latitude/longitude or escape. No relativistic planet/spacetime law is requested.'),
(5,'KEEP',[I,IV],'numerical','Binary-star orbital fraction and midpoint blackbody temperature','Equal solar-type binary orbit projection constraints determine ellipse geometry and Kepler time fractions. Inverse-square radiative flux and Stefan-Boltzmann balance give the blackbody temperature along the stipulated orbit.'),
(6,'KEEP',[I,II,VI,VII],'theory','Two Coulomb-repelling protons in a uniform magnetic field','The source explicitly neglects radiation and mutual magnetic fields. Ordinary Lorentz/Newton two-body motion, relative-coordinate energy and angular momentum give distance extrema, recurrence, circular critical speed and small perturbations.'),
(7,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','Disk rebound with an apparent normal restitution above unity','The problem asks for a two-dimensional model and defines restitution by the normal velocity component. Rotation/tangential energy or compliant-wall stored energy can feed the normal component while total energy remains conserved; an explicit lumped Newton spring/contact model suffices.'),
(8,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Bicycle front and rear tracks and a following group','No-slip wheel constraint and fixed wheelbase define an exact geometric differential equation. Solving straight/circular/sinusoidal paths and time delays through a bend is ordinary kinematics and ODE mathematics; wind-shadow motivation imposes no fluid calculation.'),
(9,'KEEP',[I],'numerical','Package transfer between synchronous stations with elastic planetary bouncers','All orbit, launch and ideal bounce conventions are supplied. Newton conic/time-of-flight matching to moving destinations and a rotating plot determine transfer speed and timing. Atmosphere escape-scale discussion remains ordinary gravity/thermal foundations.'),
(10,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','Newton motion with an explicitly proposed tensor inertia and drag','F=m*a is expressly generalized to a tensor, and central/many-body force laws plus drag are printed. Linear algebra gives rotationally invariant 2D scalar-plus-antisymmetric tensors; direct Newton ODE and conserved-quantity tests determine stationary/bounded motion. No canonical or elastic tensor law is needed.'),
(11,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','Orbital and spin exchange of a supplied two-mass rigid planet','The body is explicitly replaced by two point masses and a massless rigid rod. Newton tidal torque, total angular momentum/energy and coupled orbit/rotation equations determine transfer and possible collision with the Sun.'),
(12,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','Lowest-energy pendulum endpoint paths and large-time asymptotics','Initial/final angle and time are specified; ordinary rigid-pendulum energy quadrature and near-separatrix asymptotics supply minimal-turn solutions without quantum tunnelling or variational field laws.'),
(13,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Floating wooden sphere in a rotating tank for small and large radii','Hydrostatic pressure in the rotating effective gravity field, free-surface geometry and displaced-fluid force/torque determine equilibrium of the wooden sphere, including finite-size integrals. No viscous instability or constitutive stress tensor is required.'),
(14,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Spheroidal equilibrium of a uniformly rotating incompressible self-gravitating fluid','The source explicitly replaces the neutron star by incompressible ordinary fluid. Newton potential integration for an ellipsoid and rotating hydrostatic equipotential condition derive spheroidal equilibria and rotation/flattening limits. Relativity, nuclear equation of state and microscopic neutron physics are not required by this stipulated model.'),
(15,'KEEP',[II],'theory','Impulsive sound heard along and against a supplied linear wind shear','The velocity v=alpha*z, low wind speed, delta pulse and negligible viscosity are explicit. Ordinary sound propagation with advected wave speed and ray/wave geometry give bending, delay and focusing/shadowing; no turbulent flow closure is needed.'),
(16,'REJECT',[],'theory','Orbits and scattering in an unsupplied relativistic Lorentz-scalar dynamics','A central potential alone does not define how a Lorentz scalar modifies rest mass, relativistic energy and force. Those missing relativistic prescriptions centrally determine every orbit/potential/cross-section request despite later nonrelativistic comparisons.'),
(17,'BORDERLINE',[X],'theory','Distinguishing a fast moving-mirror image from a gas-shrouded meteor','Polarization/spectral/image reasoning can be ordinary optics, but a universal distinction at arbitrary fast motion can require unsupplied relativistic aberration/Doppler/reflection mapping. The statement supplies no operational diagnostic model and asks its failure cases; preserve the genuine whole-task ambiguity.'),
(18,'REJECT',[],'theory','Direction-dependent emission from a constantly accelerating laser','No all-speed Doppler/aberration, proper-time/frequency or accelerated-source convention is supplied. These central relativistic emission relations determine the requested direction/acceleration-dependent results; elementary stationary-source optics alone does not provide them.'),
(19,'REJECT',[],'theory','Deriving a supplied relativistic correction to Coulomb scattering','The target cross-section correction and gamma(v) are explicitly given. Relativistic momentum/energy versus velocity and trajectory/force prescriptions needed to derive that correction are not; reproducing the target formula is central and cannot be done by ordinary Rutherford substitution alone.'),
(20,'REJECT',[],'numerical','Safe circular travel near static and maximally rotating black holes','No Schwarzschild/Kerr geometry, orbit, proper acceleration or tidal-force laws are supplied. These central GR relations control closeness to the horizon/ergosphere and both mass estimates.'),
(21,'REJECT',[],'theory','Mutual visibility of radially falling black-hole observers','Observer/light trajectories, horizon causal structure and proper-frame frequency/visibility require unsupplied black-hole spacetime dynamics. No operational metric or light-propagation model is given.'),
(22,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Inverse galactic force law with a fully supplied distance-dependent Newton constant','Pair force and exponential thin-disk density are both explicitly printed. Newton superposition, radial centripetal balance and inversion of the disk force integral constrain G(r); solar-system consistency is a comparison of that same given law. No GR or unsupplied dark-matter theory is needed.'),
(23,'REJECT',[],'theory','Quantum spectrum of spherical, symmetric and asymmetric rigid rotors','Classical inertia tensor is supplied, but angular-momentum quantum representation, spectrum/degeneracy and state/superposition dynamics are not. They dominate every requested result.'),
(24,'REJECT',[],'theory','Spectrum of a matrix Hamiltonian built from a named quantum oscillator','The full matrix is supplied and can be diagonalized algebraically in terms of H0 eigenvalues. But oscillator quantum spectrum/operator representation and eigenstate interpretation are merely called well known, not provided; these outside quantum rules are central to the spectrum requested.'),
(25,'REJECT',[],'theory','Position-dependent effective-mass quantum operator orderings and interfaces','Three formal operator expressions are given, but momentum coordinate representation, Hilbert inner product, quantum boundary/current and gauge action are not operationally supplied. Those outside quantum rules centrally determine Hermiticity and interface conditions.'),
(26,'REJECT',[],'theory','Spin-orbit electron energy levels in a magnetic field','The Hamiltonian, minimal-coupling substitution and Zeeman term are supplied, but Pauli matrices are only named and quantum position/momentum commutators, Landau oscillator spectrum and eigenstate rules are not. They remain central missing quantum prerequisites.'),
(27,'REJECT',[],'theory','Whole classical rotation and quantum perturbative adiabatic-invariance task','Part a has a fully defined vector ODE and mathematical limit. Parts b/c require unsupplied first/second-order quantum time-dependent and stationary perturbation rules and their relation; these substantial central demands prevent rescuing the ordinary opening as a separate unit.'),
(28,'REJECT',[],'theory','Constrained noncommuting quantum coordinates and star products','Formal classical Hamiltonian and projection identities do not supply quantization, operator Hilbert representation, Dirac brackets or magnetic translation action. These central missing quantum methods define all constrained states, operator ordering and product calculations.'),
(29,'REJECT',[],'theory','Zero-point phonon energy and pressure in a superfluid Bose droplet','A Debye cutoff is named, but quantum mode energy/counting, interacting Bose dispersion and pressure/ground-state balance are not supplied. Those specialized quantum-fluid/statistical laws centrally determine all results.'),
(30,'KEEP',[],'theory','Ion-cloud collision-count probabilities','The many-particle short-range premise and at-least-one probability define a natural rare independent-collision Poisson limit. Probability algebra obtains the multiple-event relation under that explicit model assumption, or demonstrates why p alone is insufficient with correlations. No nuclear interaction cross-section calculation is demanded.'),
(31,'KEEP',[],'data_analysis','Testing scale-free map distributions and exponent relations','The statement asks measurements from chosen maps/databases and model construction for geometrical features. Log-scale fitting, dimensional/self-similarity models, sampling uncertainty and topology are permitted mathematical/data-analysis work; no unprovided geological dynamics is required.'),
(32,'KEEP',[I],'experimental','Unwinding paper-roll motion and breaking tension','Actual wall-contact/held-strip experiment instructions were read. Variable-radius rotational/translational Newton motion, strip mass/length conservation and tension versus an estimated/measured strength determine height and break condition in a declared ideal unwinding model; microscopic fracture mechanics is not requested.')]
u={int(r['problem_number']):r for r in c.execute('select * from units where source_file_id=3136')};assert len(u)==32 and all(r['decision'] is None for r in u.values())
pages={n:2 if n<=7 else 3 if n<=11 else 4 if n<=19 else 5 if n<=24 else 6 if n<=27 else 7 for n in range(1,33)}
out=[]
for n,d,dom,fmt,phy,reason in rows:
 out.append(dict(screening_unit_id=u[n]['screening_unit_id'],decision=d,confidence='medium' if d=='BORDERLINE' else 'high',primary_spho_domains=';'.join(dom),required_physics=phy,decision_reason=reason,external_physics_if_any=phy if d in ('BORDERLINE','REJECT') else '',format=fmt,page_start=pages[n],page_end=pages[n],visual_inspection_used=1,solution_used=0,boundary_status='content_boundary_verified',needs_second_review=n in (1,3,7,10,13,14,15,18,19,22,24,25,26,27,30,31,32),evidence=f'Complete actual Ortvay 2004 Q{n} p{pages[n]} inspected from full text and all seven cached rendered physical pages. Broken extraction does not control equation/heading interpretation. Whole parent including extra questions retained. Q1 original source-linked JPEG acquired and visually inspected separately. Organizer archive links no 2004 worked key.'))
p=w.ROOT/'reviews/shutdown_ortvay_2004_32.json';w.writejson(p,out);w.decisions(p)
image=w.ROOT/'references/ortvay_2004_q1_budapest_original.jpg';assert image.exists()
c.execute('insert into screening_references values (?,?,?,?,?,?,?,?,?)',('ortvay_2004_q1_budapest_original',u[1]['screening_unit_id'],'https://ortvay.elte.hu/2004/budapest.jpg',str(image.relative_to(w.ROOT)),w.digest(image),image.stat().st_size,None,'Original explicitly linked satellite image, essential to Q1 timing and cloud-height inference; original JPEG decoded, visually inspected and preserved without edits.',w.now()))
c.execute("update paper_boundary_audit set status='full_paper_boundaries_verified',observed_units=32,evidence=?,checked_at=? where file_id=3136",('All seven physical pages actually read: cover p1 and independent Q1-Q32 pp2-7. Extra questions in Q2/Q22 and lettered/multi-case parts remain parents. No omitted top-level task or extra task in closing TeX marker. Q1 linked image separately preserved, not another screening unit.',w.now()))
notes={1:'Original JPEG 3032x2000, 1230848 bytes, no EXIF. Shadows/clouds are present. Ground registration, projection, seasonal ambiguity, date/year prior and attainable minute precision must be evaluated; no exact time/height answer fabricated.',3:'Declare incompressible inviscid one-dimensional outlet flow; finite tube water inertia and accelerating-cart pressure must be included. Constant Torricelli speed from stationary tank is not automatically valid.',5:'Projection inclination and solar-type equal-star assumptions must be declared; projected orbit centres are not themselves the physical focus unless geometry is reconstructed.',7:'Normal restitution >1 is not total energy gain. Tangential/rotational or compliant-surface energy must be included explicitly in the permitted model.',9:'Ideal horizontal bounce exchanges momentum with rotating planet; use the surface frame. Planet mass is not explicitly fixed by matching Earth radius/period, so retain or declare a gravity parameter.',10:'In 2D rotational invariance permits a*I+b*J, not necessarily a symmetric positive scalar tensor. The antisymmetric component is allowed by the toy statement, not a real material inertia claim.',13:'Wood density, vessel dimensions, wetting and constraints are parameters; distinguish buoyant sphere position from mere free-surface minimum.',14:'Maclaurin equilibrium curve can have multiple branches. Distinguish an equilibrium angular-speed bound from a dynamical/nonaxisymmetric stability cutoff; no nuclear EOS or relativity added.',15:'Low-speed linear wind profile only applies over relevant heights; ray caustics require wave interpretation, not invented turbulence.',17:'Gas cloud expressly hides meteor shape; an apparent image alone may not uniquely identify the physical source. No actual rapid-mirror observation fabricated.',18:'Source does not specify laboratory versus proper acceleration or small-speed limit; do not silently supply a full relativity model.',19:'gamma=1/sqrt(1-v^2) and target correction are given; missing prerequisite is dynamical momentum/trajectory law, not the printed target.',22:'Actual density exponent parameter printed alpha approximately 4 kpc has wrong dimensions; alpha must be inverse length or a scale-length convention. Keep source typo and inverse-law nonuniqueness/domain limitations explicit.',24:'H0 is named as a quantum harmonic oscillator, but no En=omega*(n+1/2) or coordinate/eigenstate model is supplied.',25:'Formal expressions and usual commutation phrase do not provide coordinate representation/inner product or interface matching. A classical mass model is not a complete quantum PDE.',26:'Minimal coupling and Zeeman term genuinely supplied. Pauli matrices/quantum oscillator representation merely named, not displayed.',27:'Actual part-a limit prints omega(1/a) despite omega defined on [0,1]; intended slow argument likely omega(1). Do not silently correct. Parts b/c still require unsupplied quantum perturbation theory.',30:'p=P(N>=1) alone cannot determine P(N>=2) for arbitrary correlated/inhomogeneous counts. Poisson rare-independent limit is an explicit additional mathematical assumption, not asserted guaranteed by the source.',31:'No specific pre-supplied dataset or unique map link. Contestant chooses data and measures/fits it; this screening did not perform or fabricate geography measurements.',32:'No unwinding apparatus experiment performed. Declare no-slip/detachment/contact model, paper thickness/linear density, roll geometry and measured tensile strength; no microscopic crack law inferred.'}
for n,note in notes.items():c.execute('update units set source_quality_notes=? where screening_unit_id=?',(note,u[n]['screening_unit_id']))
c.commit();print('Saved 32 decisions, original Q1 image provenance and seven-page boundary audit.')
